{"from": "Nariway Signals <signals@nariway.com>", "to": ["alina@nariway.com"], "subject": "Nariway Signals - 2026-08-23 - the Smithsonian downsizes its own Latino museum plan", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Nariway Signals \u2014 August 23, 2026</title>\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:wght@400;500;600&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Schibsted+Grotesk:wght@500;600&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n</head>\n<body style=\"margin:0; padding:0; background-color:#FFFFFF; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"background-color:#FFFFFF; margin:0; padding:0; width:100%;\">\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:0;\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"620\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:620px; max-width:620px; margin:0 auto; padding:0;\">\n\n<!-- Masthead -->\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:48px 8px 20px 8px; text-align:center;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight:500; font-size:28px; letter-spacing:0.01em; color:#1A1A17;\">Nariway Signals</div>\n<div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.12em; color:#6B6B62; margin-top:10px;\">Sunday, August 23, 2026</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr><td style=\"padding:0 8px;\"><div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; font-size:0; line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div></td></tr>\n\n<!-- Orientation -->\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:26px 8px 8px 8px;\">\n<p style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#3A3A34; margin:0; font-style:italic;\">Heaviest today on institutions renegotiating their own ambitions against the money and politics actually available &mdash; a national museum quietly trading a purpose-built home for one it already owns, a tech fortune buying a shuttered art school back to life, and a shared campus letting several collectors each keep control of their own legacy pavilion &mdash; with the season's sharpest critique of the last big &ldquo;museum for the people&rdquo; experiment landing right as it prepares to open.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<!-- LEAD -->\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:30px 8px 6px 8px;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:11px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.12em; color:#6B6B62;\">Lead</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:6px 8px 4px 8px;\">\n<a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/smithsonian-latino-museum-arts-and-industries-building-1234795523/\" style=\"text-decoration:none; color:#1A1A17;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight:500; font-size:26px; line-height:1.28; color:#1A1A17;\">The Smithsonian's Latino museum may end up in a building it already owns, not the one Congress refused to fund.</div>\n</a>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:10px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<p style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.65; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0;\">After the House voted down the bill for a purpose-built site on the Mall in May, the Smithsonian is now weighing the 1881 Arts and Industries Building &mdash; sited between the Castle and the Hirshhorn &mdash; as the National Museum of the American Latino's home instead, sidestepping a fresh congressional fight but abandoning the board's own prior resolution to build new. A board decision is expected at the Aug 31 meeting. It's a federal-scale version of the exact tension every founder-museum in this universe eventually hits: the plan a founder (or, here, a board) first commits to is rarely the plan that survives contact with what actually gets funded.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:12px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<span style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; color:#6B6B62;\">\n<a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/smithsonian-latino-museum-arts-and-industries-building-1234795523/\" style=\"color:#6B6B62; text-decoration:underline;\">ARTnews</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/08/21/smithsonian-institution-latino-museum-arts-industries-building-washington\" style=\"color:#6B6B62; text-decoration:underline;\">The Art Newspaper</a>\n</span>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr><td style=\"padding:28px 8px 0 8px;\"><div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; font-size:0; line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div></td></tr>\n\n<!-- What's happening -->\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:26px 8px 8px 8px;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:11px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.12em; color:#6B6B62;\">What's happening</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:10px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<a href=\"https://artomipavilions.org/\" style=\"text-decoration:none; color:#1A1A17;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight:500; font-size:19px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17;\">Art Omi is building a campus where 12 to 18 collectors and artists each get to design their own legacy pavilion.</div>\n</a>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<p style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0;\">The 190-acre Chatham, NY site &mdash; Susan and Michael Hort are among the first collectors participating &mdash; is a genuinely new pathway: not one founder's museum and not a dispersal, but shared land and infrastructure with each participant controlling their own structure, in collaboration with an architect of their choosing. Phase One opens June 2027. A multi-collector answer to the single-founder-museum model this brief tracks daily.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<span style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; color:#6B6B62;\">\n<a href=\"https://artomipavilions.org/\" style=\"color:#6B6B62; text-decoration:underline;\">Art Omi Pavilions</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://www.archpaper.com/2024/07/art-omi-debuts-new-architect-and-artist-designed-pavilions-in-chatham-new-york/\" style=\"color:#6B6B62; text-decoration:underline;\">archpaper</a>\n</span>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:22px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<a href=\"https://news.vanderbilt.edu/2026/07/21/vanderbilt-to-establish-the-jen-hsun-and-lori-huang-college-of-art-architecture-and-design-in-san-francisco/\" style=\"text-decoration:none; color:#1A1A17;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight:500; font-size:19px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17;\">Catching up: Jensen and Lori Huang gave $75M to revive the shuttered California College of the Arts as a Vanderbilt-run art school.</div>\n</a>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<p style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0;\">Announced July 21 and caught late here, it's the Nvidia CEO's largest educational gift ever, and a different shape of tech wealth entering the art world than anything else in this universe &mdash; not a personal collection's museum or foundation, but money aimed at the pipeline that trains the next generation of artists and, eventually, collectors. Opens November 2027 as the Jen-Hsun and Lori Huang College of Art, Architecture and Design.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<span style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; color:#6B6B62;\">\n<a href=\"https://news.vanderbilt.edu/2026/07/21/vanderbilt-to-establish-the-jen-hsun-and-lori-huang-college-of-art-architecture-and-design-in-san-francisco/\" style=\"color:#6B6B62; text-decoration:underline;\">Vanderbilt</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/07/21/vanderbilt-university-california-college-arts-jensen-huang-gift\" style=\"color:#6B6B62; text-decoration:underline;\">The Art Newspaper</a>\n</span>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr><td style=\"padding:28px 8px 0 8px;\"><div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; font-size:0; line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div></td></tr>\n\n<!-- Worth reading -->\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:26px 8px 8px 8px;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:11px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.12em; color:#6B6B62;\">Worth reading</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:10px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<a href=\"https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/08/10/comment-george-lucas-vision-lucas-museum-narrative-art-fundraising\" style=\"text-decoration:none; color:#1A1A17;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight:500; font-size:19px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17;\">&ldquo;What happened to George Lucas's vision of a museum for &lsquo;the people&rsquo;?&rdquo;</div>\n</a>\n<div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; color:#6B6B62; margin-top:4px;\">The Art Newspaper, comment &middot; Aug 10</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<p style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0;\">A pointed critique landing five weeks before the Lucas Museum's now-firm Sept 22 opening: the museum's tiered membership and admission pricing, up to $600 a year, sit uneasily against Lucas's own framing of narrative art as belonging to everyone. Worth holding against the opening-date excitement &mdash; the sharpest available counter-read on whether the museum will actually be the &ldquo;people's&rdquo; institution its founder describes.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<span style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; color:#6B6B62;\">\n<a href=\"https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/08/10/comment-george-lucas-vision-lucas-museum-narrative-art-fundraising\" style=\"color:#6B6B62; text-decoration:underline;\">The Art Newspaper</a>\n</span>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr><td style=\"padding:28px 8px 0 8px;\"><div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; font-size:0; line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div></td></tr>\n\n<!-- To see -->\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:26px 8px 8px 8px;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:11px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.12em; color:#6B6B62;\">To see &mdash; escalating</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:10px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<a href=\"https://phxart.org/phoenix-art-museum-receives-major-gift-indigenous-artworks/\" style=\"text-decoration:none; color:#1A1A17;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight:500; font-size:19px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17;\">Phoenix Art Museum's <em>The Way We Came: A Century of Indigenous Art</em> opens Aug 26 &mdash; three days out.</div>\n</a>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<p style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0;\">Built around the William P. Healey Collection's 185-work gift, the largest gift of Native American art in the museum's 65-year history (99 artists, 44 tribal nations), assembled over a decade with Din&eacute; artist Tony Abeyta advising. A living collector's collection entering public life in real time; the exhibition runs through July 11, 2027.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<span style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; color:#6B6B62;\">\n<a href=\"https://phxart.org/phoenix-art-museum-receives-major-gift-indigenous-artworks/\" style=\"color:#6B6B62; text-decoration:underline;\">Phoenix Art Museum</a>\n</span>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:22px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/christies-alan-medaugh-hiroshige-collection-auction-1234794665/\" style=\"text-decoration:none; color:#1A1A17;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight:500; font-size:19px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17;\">Christie's Alan Medaugh Hiroshige preview is now 19 days out.</div>\n</a>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<p style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0;\">Public preview Sept 11&ndash;14, sale Sept 15, at 20 Rockefeller Plaza &mdash; already on Alina's calendar for the Sept 12 preview. The continuing countdown.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:8px 8px 0 8px;\">\n<span style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; color:#6B6B62;\">\n<a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/christies-alan-medaugh-hiroshige-collection-auction-1234794665/\" style=\"color:#6B6B62; text-decoration:underline;\">ARTnews</a>\n</span>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<!-- Footer -->\n<tr><td style=\"padding:40px 8px 0 8px;\"><div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; font-size:0; line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:20px 8px 48px 8px; text-align:center;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; color:#6B6B62; line-height:1.6;\">Nariway Signals &middot; the continuous-sensing function for private collections, legacy, and the market</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}